KZ3 patch 1158 (SPU pass 147; upstream candidate): let registered one-way entries reset a resident job overlay's lifted host stack.

A WWS job can branch from interpreted code back into a lifted entry that replaces the guest call stack. The existing
stack-reset registry handled ordinary lifted workloads, but excluded policy contexts and checked only the generic
spu_indirect_branch wrapper when an interpreter handoff resolved a lifted target. Tools of Destruction's overlay image
207 consequently re-entered 0x7808 from 0x1FA70 without unwinding, reached the host-depth guard at 2,000 calls and
stopped Zordoom Prison and Meridian City from drawing.

Permit registered resets while a policy context has a resident job overlay, and check the resolved lifted function at
the interpreter handoff. Policy code without an overlay remains excluded. The title's lift configuration registers the
verified one-way entry; unregistered transfers retain the existing behavior.

Test: tools/test_spu_interpreter_handoff.py --overlay-stack-reset drives interpreted code through a branch to a
registered lifted entry while a host call frame is live. It requires depth zero for a resident overlay and depth one
for the same transfer in a plain policy context. The focused fixture runs natively on Windows as well as POSIX.
Direct no-input starts of Zordoom Prison and Meridian City then kept presenting and drawing for 120 seconds and exited
cleanly; Meridian City progressed into the return to Fastoon.

